(function(payload){if(typeof applySerialChapterPayload==="function")applySerialChapterPayload(payload);else (window.SERIAL_CHAPTER_QUEUE||(window.SERIAL_CHAPTER_QUEUE=[])).push(payload);})({"id":"serial-cultivation-06","version":"0a6b940755c1","book":"mountain-ledger","cn":["第六日清晨，石门上的两孔恰好容下铜匙与银扣。沈砚照旧图的[[procedure|程序]]旋转，门却只升起半尺。顾衡先爬进去，随即传来一声带着惊喜的[[outcry|呼喊]]。沈砚塞住木楔，罗清举灯，让光[[penetrate|穿透]]门内的黑暗。[[damp|潮湿的]]墙壁上，水珠不断滴落，药田却一滴也得不到。铁栏后，十几名工人正轮流踩动水车，将泉水送上韩长老的石台。顾衡跪在其中一人身旁，唤了一声弟弟，久久没听见回答。","顾峦喉咙肿着，只能贴着哥哥的耳边[[murmur|低语]]。工头拦住要砸轮轴的沈砚：石台蓄气已满，忽然停转，灵力可能[[erupt|爆发]]。工人服药后难言，便被留在这里继续做活；水车的铁链还吊着内闸。罗清先把能走的人与重伤者[[isolate|分隔开]]，免得堵住窄门，再请大家[[cooperate|合作]]搬人。顾峦抬手指向链槽，顾衡才放下剑，跟着他一点点松开卡住衣角的铁环。没人能靠一击砸碎所有麻烦。","门轴呻吟，沈砚盯着粗链上的[[tension|张力]]，发现它同时牵动两道门。壁上的[[diagram|示意图]]原本用两股支流保持灵力的[[equilibrium|平衡]]，直到石台将一边截走。银扣对着旧槽微微发亮，被废弃的那道支流还活着。图上没有沈家的名字，也没有所谓天定血脉；只要守户将修为送进槽口，便能[[activate|启动]]闸轴。母亲留下的不是只认儿子的宝物，而是一份谁都可以接手的工作。他将受伤的手放到身后，试着用右掌供力。","上方传来韩长老的声音。他承认把有限的水源[[resource|资源]]送上石台，是为了抵挡西来的匪患；十二年前，他的小儿子死在那里。沈砚说，孩子渴死在山下也不是保护。长老许诺归还药田，保证他通过考核，只要交出两把钥匙，别浪费自己的[[potential|潜力]]。这份[[temptation|诱惑]]并非全无分量，沈砚看了一眼疼得握不拢的左手，随后问：能否把这笔交换写进公开的[[register|登记册]]，让山下各家也读一遍？长老的脸色沉了下去。","内闸忽然下落。顾衡背起顾峦，罗清扶人钻向外门。沈砚把银扣插入旧侧槽，耗去修为撑住水压，木楔上的压力才逐渐[[lessen|减轻]]。十五名工人逃出后，他也跌进门外的泥里。这不是一场毫无代价的胜仗：修行遭到[[setback|挫折]]，倒退了半个[[realm|境界]]，铜匙还留在门上，被长老的人夺走。沈砚喝着罗清递来的水，开始[[assess|评估]]下一步。人出来了，主闸却仍掌在别人手中，山下的田还要等。"],"en":["On the sixth morning, the two holes in the stone door accepted the copper key and silver clasp. Shen followed the turning [[procedure|procedure]] on the drawing, but the door rose only half a foot. Gu crawled under first. An excited [[outcry|outcry]] followed. Shen secured a wooden wedge while Luo raised her lamp, letting the light [[penetrate|penetrate]] the darkness. Water dripped constantly down the [[damp|damp]] walls, yet none reached the fields. Behind iron bars, more than a dozen workers took turns driving a waterwheel that supplied Han's platform. Gu knelt beside one of them and called him his brother. For a long time, no answer came.","Gu Luan's throat was swollen. He could only [[murmur|murmur]] into his brother's ear. The foreman stopped Shen from smashing the axle. The platform's stored energy was full; a sudden stop might make it [[erupt|erupt]]. Unable to speak clearly after taking the medicine, the workers had been kept there to continue working. The wheel's chain also supported the inner gate. Luo began to [[isolate|isolate]] those able to walk from the badly injured so the narrow exit would not jam. She asked everyone to [[cooperate|cooperate]] in carrying patients. Gu Luan pointed toward the chain groove. Gu lowered his sword and carefully freed an iron ring trapping his brother's clothing. No single blow could break all their troubles.","The door shaft groaned. Watching the chain's [[tension|tension]], Shen realized it controlled both doors. The wall [[diagram|diagram]] showed two branches maintaining an [[equilibrium|equilibrium]] of energy before the platform diverted one. The clasp glowed faintly against the old groove. The abandoned branch still worked. The drawing contained no family name and no chosen bloodline. Any keeper could feed cultivated strength into the groove to [[activate|activate]] the shaft. His mother's legacy was not a treasure that recognized only her son; it was a task someone else could take over. He put his injured hand behind him and tried supplying energy through his right palm.","Han spoke from above. He admitted directing the limited water [[resource|resource]] to the platform to resist western bandits. His youngest son had died there twelve years earlier. Shen said children dying of thirst below was no protection either. Han offered the field and a guaranteed examination pass if Shen surrendered the keys instead of wasting his [[potential|potential]]. The [[temptation|temptation]] had weight. Shen glanced at his left hand, which hurt too much to close. Then he asked whether the exchange could be written in the public [[register|register]] for the valley households to read. Han's expression darkened.","The inner gate suddenly descended. Gu carried his brother, and Luo helped the others toward the outer door. Shen fitted the clasp into the old side groove and spent his own energy resisting the water pressure. Only then did the force on the wedge [[lessen|lessen]]. After fifteen workers escaped, he fell into the mud outside. This was no victory without a price. His cultivation suffered a [[setback|setback]], losing half a [[realm|realm]] of progress. The copper key remained in the door, where Han's men took it. Drinking water Luo handed him, Shen began to [[assess|assess]] their next step. The workers were out, but someone else still controlled the main gate. The fields below had to wait."]});
